      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.046,
            0.364,
            0.064
          ],
          "content": "Ganita Prakash | Grade 7"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.088,
            0.847,
            0.125
          ],
          "content": "a concise way. Mathematical relations expressed this way are often called formulas."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.134,
            0.293,
            0.157
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Figure it Out"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.162,
            0.16,
            0.553,
            0.18
          ],
          "content": "1. Write formulas for the perimeter of:"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.206,
            0.184,
            0.537,
            0.204
          ],
          "content": "(a) triangle with all sides equal."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.207,
            0.209,
            0.848,
            0.265
          ],
          "content": "(b) a regular pentagon (as we have learnt last year, we use the word ‘regular’ to say that all sidelengths and angle measures are equal)"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.208,
            0.269,
            0.44,
            0.289
          ],
          "content": "(c) a regular hexagon"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.163,
            0.294,
            0.848,
            0.369
          ],
          "content": "2. Munirathna has a 20 m long pipe. However, he wants a longer watering pipe for his garden. He joins another pipe of some length to this one. Give the expression for the combined length of the pipe. Use the letter-number ‘k’ to denote the length in meters of the other pipe."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.163,
            0.372,
            0.848,
            0.412
          ],
          "content": "3. What is the total amount Krithika has, if she has the following numbers of notes of ₹100, ₹20 and ₹5? Complete the following table:"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "bbox": [
            0.173,
            0.416,
            0.823,
            0.663
          ],
          "content": "| No. of₹100 notes | No. of₹20 notes | No. of₹5 notes | Expression and totalamount |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| 3 | 5 | 6 |  |\n|  |  |  | $\\begin{array}{c}6 \\times 100 + 4 \\times 20 + 3 \\times 5 \\\\= 695\\end{array}$ |\n| 8 | 4 | Z |  |\n| X | y | Z |  |",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_3_table_9.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.162,
            0.679,
            0.848,
            0.773
          ],
          "content": "4. Venkatalakshmi owns a flour mill. It takes 10 seconds for the roller mill to start running. Once it is running, each kg of grain takes 8 seconds to grind into powder. Which of the expressions below describes the time taken to complete grind ‘y’ kg of grain, assuming the machine is off initially?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.206,
            0.776,
            0.677,
            0.798
          ],
          "content": "$1 0 + 8 + y$ (b) $( 1 0 \\pm 8 ) \\times y$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.207,
            0.801,
            0.665,
            0.822
          ],
          "content": "$1 0 \\times 8 \\times y$ (d) $1 0 + 8 \\times y$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.208,
            0.825,
            0.352,
            0.845
          ],
          "content": "(e) $1 0 \\times y + 8$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.163,
            0.849,
            0.745,
            0.87
          ],
          "content": "5. Write algebraic expressions using letters of your choice."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.207,
            0.874,
            0.483,
            0.893
          ],
          "content": "(a) 5 more than a number"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.208,
            0.898,
            0.467,
            0.917
          ],
          "content": "(b) 4 less than a number"
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.159,
